{"key":"eJwVjMEOgyAQRL\/GoywgKvbWS\/9jZUGbIlDZpu3flyZzmJfJm5251AsAJrfnU4QDKozeW7KLgZLJYWUoEb9gzCRnKSXsf6Ubrp2+tdDg+BOf6sFvnaJwMb8onDmxSJ7bXhm3e9pa01KrXuleLg2CXacpoF5QDXO7peBXCjQ7Qm39GMRh8AeAgDEl","enclosureUrl":"https:\/\/anchor.fm\/s\/5ee8d894\/podcast\/play\/44607000\/https%3A%2F%2Fd3ctxlq1ktw2nl.cloudfront.net%2Fstaging%2F2021-12-09%2Ff8b66fa29a137700dfebdfd7cda28e5f.m4a","enclosureType":"audio\/x-m4a","enclosureLen":"13518521","title_ep":"Universities: The Frontline of the Culture War. With the Honorable Kat Cammack (FL-03)","description_ep":"<p>Join Cherise as she and Congresswoman Kat Cammack (FL-03) discuss the disconcerting role universities play in our current culture war and how universities are becoming training grounds for far-left progressivism. It&nbsp;is becoming increasingly clear that what happens on campus does not stay on campus. Students are taking these toxic environments and are reproducing them in their places of work and their communities putting universities right at the frontline of the culture war.<\/p>\n","pubDate_ep":"Thu, 09 Dec 2021 18:00:00 GMT","author_ep":null,"guid_ep":{"text":"5601d021-827a-4a1a-9768-57f4dd04fc04","isPermaLink":"false"},"duration_ep":"00:13:55","language_ep":null,"epHasPol":true,"polGuestName":"kat cammack","rssKey":896212,"title_pod":"Well Said","description_pod":"Well Said is hosted by Cherise Trump, Executive Director of Speech First. Each episode is a deep dive into issues around free speech, higher education, and other related topics such as American culture and society. Cherise holds conversation-style interviews with her guests who range from experts on law and policy to activists, students, and professors who are fighting censorship and coercion on campuses. Join us for a show that prioritizes bringing issues to the public and emphasizing that what happens on campus, does not stay on campus. To learn more, visit www.speechfirst.org.","lastBuildDate_pod":"Tue, 13 May 2025 09:58:14 GMT","language_pod":"en","